ndings":[{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"summarize_clone catches only telemetry._Unreadable. An events.jsonl line that is valid JSON but not an object (for example [1, 2]) makes _finished_at, _terminal, and _hosted call .get on a list and raise AttributeError; a finding with a list severity raises TypeError in the tally. The scan runs in the fallback and in the unmirrored check, including under --all-repos inside a clone, so one bad record turns the report into internal_error instead of an unreadable entry.","fix_commit":"263e9b54d5b052669399c99cee365620f271c583","id":"F001","line":203,"path":"agentic_preflight/report.py","response_note":null,"severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Catch any other exception from _summarize_stored_run in summarize_clone and record the run in unreadable_runs with reason 'invalid' and a diagnostic that names only the exception type. Add a test with a non-object event line.","title":"A record with a non-object event or finding fails the whole report","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"findings.total, blocking.total, and the fix-commit and restart totals are sums over observed runs, so they are 0 when no run in a group has the value. The group tables in the Markdown show findings.total with no denominator, so a repository whose runs have no findings file reads as '0 findings'. That presents unknown as zero, which the summary contract forbids.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F002","line":468,"path":"agentic_preflight/report.py","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Return null for those totals when no run was observed, and render n/a in the Markdown.","title":"Unknown findings totals render as zero","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"_dedupe keys on (root_commit or source_worktree_path, run_id). A run whose row was written once without a root commit and once with one has two keys, and belongs_to_clone matches both, so the run counts twice and appears in two repository groups.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":132,"path":"agentic_preflight/report.py","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"After the key dedupe, collapse rows with the same run_id, created_at, and source_worktree_path to the newest written_at and count them in duplicates.","title":"One run mirrored under two identity keys is counted twice","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The docs and the next instruction say malformed_lines lists the malformed lines, but only the first MALFORMED_LINE_LIMIT are listed. The docs say dedupe works as in telemetry rebuild, but the report dedupes only lines that validate as summaries, so it can keep an older valid row where rebuild keeps a newer line.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F004","line":562,"path":"skill/reference/commands.md","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Say that malformed_lines lists the first 20 and that malformed counts all of them; say that only valid summary rows are deduplicated.","title":"malformed_lines and dedupe are described more broadly than the code behaves","unit":"U0010"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"Matching by name keeps every repository with that name, for example two forks named widget.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F005","line":121,"path":"docs/local-telemetry.md","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Write that --repo keeps the repositories whose name or remote matches.","title":"--repo is described as keeping one repository","unit":"U0007"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The reference says each ratio has numerator and each statistic reports excluded_runs. blocking.fixed_share has numerator_min and numerator_max, and the stage and hosted exclusions are attempts_excluded_runs, reused_excluded_runs, and pr_url_excluded_runs.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F006","line":590,"path":"skill/reference/commands.md","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Name the actual fields.","title":"Documented ratio and exclusion field names do not match every statistic","unit":"U0010"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"If a rebuild cannot add a run (for example a record whose clone has no root commit and whose worktree was removed), report names rebuild again and an agent that follows next.command loops.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F007","line":189,"path":"skill/reference/playbooks.md","response_note":"Fixed in repair commit 263e9b5 together with F001. That commit is now the reviewed snapshot, so respond cannot attach it as a new in-place repair commit for this finding.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Tell the agent to run rebuild once per clone and to report the remaining gap to the user if report still names it.","title":"Playbook has no stop condition when a rebuild does not close the gap","unit":"U0011"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The pipe-esc